# GD-28 (the user, 2026-10-29; writer 10): L §2.4 "Two rules, or two items, that every key above leaves tied (two
# rows with no start, two rows read `after m`, two rows with one start, a `same` item and a row of its target and
# keys) sort by their own canonical line, compared as ASCII". Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §2.4. The old comment:
# GD-24 (round 19, writer 10): "Ties L §2.4 still leaves (two rows with no start, two `after m` rows, two rows with one
# start) stay REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED where met" (faults5 item 9). L §2.4 sorts version items "... then by the start of their
# own governs span or their instant (a row with no span of its own first, then a span with no start, a row governing
# always among them, then by start; a row read after m after the dated ones of its target and keys)".
# Two rows of y, one governing ..2026, one always: both spans with no start.
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input y: int

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  y = 1 governs ..2026
  replace y = 2 governs always
